<title>YEMEN: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>YEMEN GOVERNMENT LIST (970519)</p>
<p>  ***********************************************************</p>
<p>  * 17 May 97 - A new government, lead by Prime Minister    *</p>
<p>  *		 Faraj Said Bin Ghanem, was sworn in by	*</p>
<p>  *		 President Ali Abdullah Saleh.		   *</p>
<p>  ***********************************************************</p>
<p> President............................Ali Abdullah SALEH (GPC)</p>
<p>  (Re-elected 1 Oct 94 for further 5-year term)</p>
<p> Vice-president...................Abd-Rabbu Mansour HADI (GPC)</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Prime Minister............Faraj Said BIN GHANEM (Independent)</p>
<p>  (Apptd 14 May 97)</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister &amp;</p>
<p>     Minister of Foreign Affairs...Abdul-Karim al-IRYANI (GPC)</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Agriculture &amp;</p>
<p>	 Water Resources.............Ahmad Salem al-JABALI (GPC)</p>
<p> Civil Administration ..........Mohammad Ahmad al-JUNAID (GPC)</p>
<p> Communications................. .Ahmad Mohammad al-ANSI (GPC)</p>
<p> Culture &amp; Tourism...................Abdul-Malek MANSOUR (GPC)</p>
<p> Defence ....................Mohammad Deifallah MOHAMMAD (GPC)</p>
<p> Education....................Yahya Mohammad al-SHOUAIBI (GPC)</p>
<p> Electricity and Water..................Ali Hamid SHARAF (GPC)</p>
<p> Expatriate Affairs.........Abdullah Saleh SABAA (Independent)</p>
<p> Finance...........................Alawi Saleh AS-SALAMI (GPC)</p>
<p> Fisheries.........................Ahmad Mousaed HUSSEIN (GPC)</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs.................................see Deputy PM</p>
<p> Health...............Abdullah Abdul-Wali NASHER (Independent)</p>
<p> Housing &amp; Urban Planning......Abdullah Hussein AD-DAFEI (GPC)</p>
<p> Industry..........................Ahmad Mohammad SOUFAN (GPC)</p>
<p> Information........................Abdurahman al-AKAWAA (GPC)</p>
<p> Interior..........................Hussein Mohammad ARAB (GPC)</p>
<p> Justice...........................Ismail Ahmed al-Wazir (GPC)</p>
<p> Legal &amp; Parliamentary Affairs.....Abdullah Ahmad GHANEM (GPC)</p>
<p> Local Administration..................Sadeq Amin ABURAS (GPC)</p>
<p> Minister of State</p>
<p>	for Prime Ministry Affairs....Ahmed Ali al-BISHARI (GPC)</p>
<p> Oil &amp; Mineral Resources.....Mohammad al-Khadem AL-WAJIH (GPC)</p>
<p> Planning &amp; Development.............Abdul-Qader BAGAMMAL (GPC)</p>
<p> Religious Guidance..............Ahmad Mohammad al-SHAMI (Haq)</p>
<p> Social Affairs &amp; Welfare....Mohammad Abdullah AL-BITANI (GPC)</p>
<p> Supply &amp; Trade.........Abdul-Rahman Mohammad Ali OTHMAN (GPC)</p>
<p> Transport.........................Abdul-Malek AL-SAYANI (GPC)</p>
<p> Youth &amp; Sports........................Abdul-Wahab RAWEH (GPC)</p>
<p> Labour &amp; Vocational Training.........Mohammad Al-TAYYEB (GPC)</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor............Ahmad Abdul-Rahman al-SAMAWI</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>PARTY AFFILIATIONS:</p>
<p> GPC    - General People's Congress headed by President Saleh</p>
<p> Haq    - Haq (Shi'ite Islamist party)</p>
